Description: download manager for files, videos and torrents
 LDM is a download manager for Linux, inspired by 1DM for Android:
 multi-part downloads with pause, resume and retry, video and stream
 downloads (yt-dlp), torrents (libtorrent), a scheduler, desktop
 notifications and a browser extension for Firefox, Chrome and Brave.
 Downloads run in a background service, so closing the window never
 stops them.
 .
 The package includes a copy of yt-dlp, used when it is newer than the
 system's; LDM keeps a per-user copy up to date as well.
